/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  pumpSystem01_operating_point
  ============================

  A pump and its piping system IN SERIES, swept over the feed flow (see
  system/outerDict).  The classical operating-point construction:

    * PUMP characteristic -- the shaft delivers a FIXED 2 kW at eta 0.65,
      so the pressure rise FALLS with flow:  dP_pump = eta W / Q_vol.
      This is the constant-shaft-power characteristic of the pump MODEL,
      not a manufacturer's tested H(Q) curve -- the engine says what it
      models, never pretends to a datasheet it was not given.

    * SYSTEM curve -- the same flow through 50 m of 0.1 m commercial-steel
      pipe with two elbows, a globe valve and a 2 m rise:
      dP_system = friction(Q^2) + fittings(Q^2) + rho g dz.

  Where the two curves CROSS, the pump's rise exactly pays the system's
  demand -- the operating point.  Hand estimate (water, v ~ 1.807e-5
  m3/mol, A = 7.854e-3 m2, f ~ 0.018, sum K = 11.8):

      pump:    dP ~ 1300 / (F 1.807e-5)          ~  7.19e4 / F   Pa
      system:  dP ~ 5.45e4 F^2 + 1.956e4          Pa   (F in kmol/s)
      cross:   F* ~ 0.99 kmol/s  (~3.6e3 kmol/h), dP* ~ 0.73 bar

  The sweep straddles that crossing (0.4..1.6 kmol/s); each point is a
  complete converged pass, and the curves are read off the pump's and the
  pipe's own published KPIs -- nothing is fitted or interpolated here.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        pump01;
        type        pump;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( mid );

        operation
        {
            W_shaft   2.0  kW;           // hardware: motor power (FIXED across the sweep)
            eta       0.65;              // pump efficiency
        }
    }

    {
        name        P1;
        type        pipe;
        model       Churchill;          // one explicit friction correlation, all regimes
        in          mid;
        outputs     ( delivered );

        operation
        {
            geometry
            {
                D          0.1     m;    // internal diameter
                L          50.0    m;    // straight length
                roughness  4.6e-5  m;    // commercial steel
                dz         2.0     m;    // outlet 2 m above inlet (static head)

                fittings
                (
                    { K 0.9;  count 2; }   // two 90-degree elbows
                    { K 10.0;          }   // one globe valve, fully open
                );
            }
        }
    }
);
